  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Bae Systems Space and Mission Systems obligated $285M in FY2026 to date across 62 awards, with an average award size of $4.6M and obligations up 32.6% year over year. National Aeronautics and Space Administration is the largest buyer, accounting for $230M of obligations, followed by the Department of Defense with $52.7M. Engineering Services is the largest market by obligations at $140M, followed by Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $66.1M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $55.1M. Historical annual obligations show variation by fiscal year: FY21 $328M, FY22 $205M, FY23 $240M, FY24 $202M, FY25 $215M, and FY26 $285M. Smaller FY2026 obligations are recorded in other markets and agencies, including Department of Commerce $2.1M, Department of the Interior $128K, and Department of Homeland Security $0. The current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date, and the largest product and service categories are concentrated in engineering, missile and space vehicle manufacturing, and physical sciences R and D.",
    "sections": [
